# Logs — operational data, don't commit
data/logs/

# OS junk
.DS_Store

# JetBrains (PHPStorm/IntelliJ) — can contain deployment hostnames/credentials
.idea/

# The deploy script. It holds no credential — the GVFS SFTP mount it writes to is already
# authenticated when you mount it, and the script says so in its own header. What it does hold is
# the Strato account name and host, which are infrastructure identifiers this repository is public
# enough not to want.
#
# Know what that costs, because it is not nothing: deploy.sh is the *recovery path* for a push that
# breaks src/, and it therefore exists on exactly one machine and in no repository. If that matters
# more than the two identifiers do, the fix is to commit it with those read from the environment.
deploy.sh

# Pre-public site auth — dot-prefix the file to disable the gate without losing it
data/site_auth.php
data/.site_auth.php

# Demos — unreleased tracks behind a per-demo password. Gitignored because `origin` is a public
# GitHub repository and these name work that is not out yet: demos.php carries the titles and the
# bcrypt hashes, data/demos/ carries the audio itself.
#
# NOT excluded from deploy.sh, and the pair is deliberate: rsync copies data/ from the working tree
# without consulting git, so both still reach the server. The credentials files above are the
# opposite arrangement — they are excluded there because the repo copies are placeholders.
data/demos.php
data/demos/

# Composer dev dependencies (PHPUnit) — dev-only, never deployed
/vendor/
.phpunit.cache/
.php-cs-fixer.cache

# npm dev dependencies (TypeScript) — same deal, dev-only and never deployed. The *compiled*
# JS in public/assets/js/ is committed on purpose, and no longer for the reason this said: deploy.sh
# ships build/dist/public/ now, not public/, so a gitignored build output would not deploy a site
# with no JS. Three other things read that tree by path and all three break without it — test/js/
# imports the modules, `npm run coverage` pins its 100% gate to public/assets/js/**, and the verify
# script diffs it byte-for-byte against a fresh tsc. See CLAUDE.md's "Debug and prod builds".
/node_modules/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Scratch outDir for the verify script's "compiled output is current" check
/.tscheck/

# Scratch dir for the verify script's asset-manifest drift check
/.assetcheck/

# phpactor writes this on first attach; editor state, not project config
.phpactor.json

# Merged coverage reports (composer coverage), and build/dist/ — the prod tree deploy.sh ships.
# Generated on demand by `npm run build:prod`, never committed: what is committed is the readable
# public/ the tests and the drift check read.
/build/

# The update endpoint's public key, and the serial it has last accepted.
#
# The key is per-deployment — that is what binds a signed payload to one server without any field
# in the manifest naming one — and its *absence* is the off switch: no key, no endpoint. So a
# clone starts closed rather than open, which is the opposite polarity to data/site_auth.php above
# and worth reading twice. deploy.sh excludes it too; upload it by hand, once.
#
# The private half is never here at all. It lives at ~/.config/neurosys/update.key, outside the
# repository entirely, the way the SoundCloud refresh token does.
data/update.pub
/.update-serial
